  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44988281",
      "title": "Git Version Control",
      "lectureOrder": 448,
      "videoOrder": 447,
      "sourceHash": "94a2ec5108933b5aac121fed35eae1b6043da31890f28c36d315ac13f74eeae1",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "-: Git is a distributed version control system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 6.87,
          "en": "Now the problem is if you want to understand Git,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.87,
          "end": 9.33,
          "en": "you have to first understand what do you mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.33,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "by version control, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 13.74,
          "en": "And then we can discuss about version control system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.74,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "then we can discuss about why it's called distributed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 19.26,
          "en": "and then Git will make much more sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 21.78,
          "en": "So let's talk about version control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.78,
          "end": 23.34,
          "en": "See, the thing is, when you make a project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.34,
          "end": 24.75,
          "en": "of course it can be any project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.75,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "it can be a software project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 29.58,
          "en": "or it can be writing a book or making videos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.58,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "It's all about a project, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 32.64,
          "en": "And when you make a project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "the way you work is you create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 35.85,
          "en": "different versions of it, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 35.85,
          "end": 37.56,
          "en": "Okay, so if you don't want to say version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 37.56,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "let's say you make multiple updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 41.31,
          "en": "So when I start writing a book,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 41.31,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "I will write something, and then I will edit the same file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 46.343,
          "en": "or maybe I want to go back to my previous file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 46.343,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "So let's say if I'm writing chapter one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 50.22,
          "en": "I will complete that chapter one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 50.22,
          "end": 52.62,
          "en": "and then I will go for chapter two, chapter three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 52.62,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "Now, at every chapter end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 56.61,
          "en": "I will just try to save it, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 56.61,
          "end": 57.84,
          "en": "And then on, on chapter two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 57.84,
          "end": 59.97,
          "en": "I will try to save a file on chapter three,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 59.97,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "I want to save a file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "or maybe while writing this chapter in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 65.67,
          "en": "I will do the save, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 67.38,
          "en": "And saving is very important, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 67.38,
          "end": 68.76,
          "en": "Otherwise, if your laptop crashes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 68.76,
          "end": 70.44,
          "en": "you will lose all the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 75.44,
          "en": "So as a writer, we normally say Ctrl+S not once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 77.543,
          "en": "multiple times, just to be on the safe side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 77.543,
          "end": 82.44,
          "en": "The important part here is we want to make the copies of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 82.44,
          "end": 83.97,
          "en": "Now, there are multiple ways of doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 83.97,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "What you can do is you can save the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 88.92,
          "en": "The thing is, if you save the same file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 88.92,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "you will lose the previous file, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 93.42,
          "en": "Or what you can do is you can create a new file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 93.42,
          "end": 97.35,
          "en": "So every new update will be a new file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 97.35,
          "end": 99.36,
          "en": "And as a software developer, we used to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 99.36,
          "end": 100.894,
          "en": "In my college days,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 100.894,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "I remember when we used to create project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 104.7,
          "en": "every time we add a new feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "we used to create a new folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "And let me know if you have done this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 111,
          "en": "or maybe you can just give a smile if you have done this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "We create a project and then we give a name to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 116.00999999999999,
          "en": "Let's say the project is for a quiz application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 116.00999999999999,
          "end": 117.87,
          "en": "So you will say quiz app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 117.87,
          "end": 119.53999999999999,
          "en": "And then if you think this is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 119.53999999999999,
          "end": 121.41,
          "en": "now we have added few features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 121.41,
          "end": 125.338,
          "en": "We can say quiz app one, quiz app two, quiz app three.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 125.338,
          "end": 128.31,
          "en": "Of course it'll have a new updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 128.31,
          "end": 130.77,
          "en": "new features in that particular new folder, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 130.77,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "And then the moment you feel that project is complete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 135.54,
          "en": "you say quiz app final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 135.54,
          "end": 139.2,
          "en": "then you say quiz app, final final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 142.14,
          "en": "because maybe you want to make some final changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 142.14,
          "end": 144.12,
          "en": "And then you realize, oh, there's a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 144.12,
          "end": 147.57,
          "en": "Then you say quiz app final final final, very final.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 147.57,
          "end": 150.003,
          "en": "Okay, so this is the type of folder we used to create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 150.003,
          "end": 152.04,
          "en": "The thing is, why do we do this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 152.04,
          "end": 153.6,
          "en": "It's because what if you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 155.183,
          "en": "to go back to the previous version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 155.183,
          "end": 158.82,
          "en": "What if you have created a project and then it's working,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 160.323,
          "en": "and now you added new features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 160.323,
          "end": 163.05,
          "en": "and then you thought it is working, but it's not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 163.05,
          "end": 164.4,
          "en": "There are some bugs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 164.4,
          "end": 167.82,
          "en": "You may want to go back to the previous version, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 167.82,
          "end": 171.21,
          "en": "Now having that version called or having that power,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 171.21,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "or going back to any version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 175.26,
          "en": "that is called version control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 175.26,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "And to achieve this, we need to use some softwares, right,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 180.36,
          "en": "some system, and that system is called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 180.36,
          "end": 182.4,
          "en": "a version control system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 182.4,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "So example, if you're building a project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 186.51,
          "en": "you will be saving that file multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 186.51,
          "end": 188.82,
          "en": "and then you will not replace the older project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 190.83,
          "en": "The older project will be there, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 190.83,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "So let's say you have a software with X number of features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "So you got the first two feature in the first version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 198.75,
          "en": "then you got the third feature on the second version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 200.13,
          "en": "And at any given point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 200.13,
          "end": 202.56,
          "en": "you can go back to the previous version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 202.56,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "Also, what if you are not alone in the project?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 207.54,
          "en": "You have multiple people working in the same project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 207.54,
          "end": 208.47899999999998,
          "en": "How do you collaborate?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 208.47899999999998,
          "end": 209.876,
          "en": "That's also important, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 209.876,
          "end": 211.679,
          "en": "So you will get those features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 211.679,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "with the help of version control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 215.4,
          "en": "And as I mentioned before, you need a system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 215.4,
          "end": 218.46,
          "en": "So we call it as a version control system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 218.46,
          "end": 219.85399999999998,
          "en": "Now, when you talk about version control system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 219.85399999999998,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "we can categorize into three parts here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 224.22,
          "en": "The first one is a local version control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 224.22,
          "end": 226.473,
          "en": "which simply means that as a developer or as a creator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 226.473,
          "end": 229.654,
          "en": "if I write softwares or if I write a book,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 229.654,
          "end": 231.03,
          "en": "if I write something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 231.03,
          "end": 233.07,
          "en": "and if I want to save in my own machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 233.07,
          "end": 234.414,
          "en": "with different versions, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 234.414,
          "end": 236.31,
          "en": "that is local copy, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 236.31,
          "end": 238.26,
          "en": "And in my own particular machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 238.26,
          "end": 239.57999999999998,
          "en": "I'm creating different versions of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 239.57999999999998,
          "end": 242.28,
          "en": "Maybe having a folder inside a folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 242.28,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "then having different folders of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 246.12,
          "en": "Or maybe I can just create a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 246.12,
          "end": 247.68,
          "en": "where I will save all these files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 247.68,
          "end": 248.91,
          "en": "Again, that's my choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 248.91,
          "end": 251.04,
          "en": "or that's depends upon the version control system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 251.04,
          "end": 253.74,
          "en": "But the thing is, everything is happening on my machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 253.74,
          "end": 256.65,
          "en": "The problem here is what if I want to collaborate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 256.65,
          "end": 257.82,
          "en": "with other people?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 257.82,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "I have, let's say, five people in the team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 261.701,
          "en": "and we all want to work on the same project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 261.701,
          "end": 262.823,
          "en": "How will we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 262.823,
          "end": 266.61,
          "en": "And also, what if I'm relying on my machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 266.61,
          "end": 269.797,
          "en": "and then one day, my machine says, \"Okay, I'm done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 269.797,
          "end": 271.68,
          "en": "\"I'm not going to start again.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 271.68,
          "end": 272.88,
          "en": "How will you get your projects?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 272.88,
          "end": 276.21,
          "en": "And that's where you can't simply rely on local copy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 276.21,
          "end": 277.83,
          "en": "And that's where we have one more option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 279.423,
          "en": "which is called CVCS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 280.371,
          "end": 281.79200000000003,
          "en": "So VCS is version control system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 281.79200000000003,
          "end": 285.75,
          "en": "CVCS is your centralized version control system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 285.75,
          "end": 287.04,
          "en": "Now in this case, what you do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 287.04,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "let's say you have five people in the network,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 290.574,
          "en": "or five people want to work on the same project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 290.574,
          "end": 293.79,
          "en": "So what you will do is you will use a central repository,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 293.79,
          "end": 295.541,
